      "function": "do_uncompress_block",
      "line": 2825,
      "var": "cmask",
      "code": "const uint64_t cmask = rar->cstate.window_mask;",
      "note": "Decompression of the merged block (spanning both volumes) reads the mismatched window_mask (64MB-1) as the circular-buffer mask used for every window_buf access.",
      "role": "intermediate"
    },
    {
      "step": 7,
      "file": "libarchive/archive_read_support_format_rar5.c",
      "function": "do_uncompress_block",
      "line": 2873,
      "var": "window_buf",
      "code": "rar->cstate.window_buf[write_idx & cmask] = (uint8_t) num;",
      "note": "Sink: literal bytes are written into window_buf at (write_idx & cmask). Because cmask is 64MB-1 while window_buf is only 128KB, once write_idx reaches 128KB the write index exceeds the real buffer, producing an out-of-bounds write and a SIGSEGV.",
